    "q-28733": {
      "dom_id": "step-q28733",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "${(-{x}^{-3}y)}^{-5}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the power of product rule and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(-{x}^{-3}y)}^{-5} & = \\\\ {(-{x}^{-3})}^{-5}{(y)}^{-5} & = \\\\ (-x)^{(-3)(-5)}\\cdot {y}^{-5} & = \\\\ (-x)^{15}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{y}^{5}} & = \\\\ -\\frac{{x}^{15}}{{y}^{5}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
