      "dom_id": "step-q72556",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to ${({x}^{-2}y)}^{-3}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the power of product rule and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({x}^{-2}y)}^{-3} & = \\\\ {({x}^{-2})}^{-3}{y}^{-3} & = \\\\ {x}^{-2(-3)}\\cdot {y}^{-3} & = \\\\ {x}^{6}{y}^{-3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
